{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9SystemSetP","text":"SystemSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A system is one step of a frame or tick: moving everything with a velocity, applying damage,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting the score. You put systems in a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which runs each of them once per run,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and at the same time as one another where it can.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most systems are declared with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},{"type":"text","text":" macro, which writes the conformance from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method’s parameters. Conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"System"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself when a system needs the whole world,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example to spawn and despawn entities directly or to reach types chosen at run time. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conforming type implements "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and, so that it can run alongside other systems,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declares an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":" listing what it reads and writes:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Friction: System {","    var access: Access? { .writes(Velocity.self) }","","    func run(in world: inout World) {","        world.update(Velocity.self) { velocity, _ in","            velocity.dx *= 0.5","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let puck = world.spawn(Velocity(dx: 8, dy: 0))","Schedule { Friction() }.run(on: &world)","print(world[Velocity.self, of: puck].dx)","\/\/ Prints \"4.0\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system keeps no state of its own between runs. Anything it needs to remember belongs in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world, as components or resources, so it is copied, compared and restored along with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"everything else."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every system type is also a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet"},{"type":"text","text":" containing each of its systems, so ordering"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constraints such as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" can name it."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","interf